#. module: account_statement_reconcile_improvements
#: model:ir.model.fields,field_description:account_statement_reconcile_improvements.field_res_company__bank_statement_auto_reconcile_outstanding_only
#: model:ir.model.fields,field_description:account_statement_reconcile_improvements.field_res_config_settings__bank_statement_auto_reconcile_outstanding_only
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:account_statement_reconcile_improvements.res_config_settings_view_form
msgid "Only auto-reconcile through outstanding accounts"
msgstr ""

#. module: account_statement_reconcile_improvements
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:account_statement_reconcile_improvements.field_res_company__bank_statement_auto_reconcile_outstanding_only
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:account_statement_reconcile_improvements.field_res_config_settings__bank_statement_auto_reconcile_outstanding_only
msgid ""
"Odoo's own automatic bank reconciliation (triggered by having a contact on "
"the line - set by the CUIT match on import, or manually) can match a "
"statement line directly against an open invoice/bill's receivable/payable "
"account, skipping the outstanding payment/receipt (\"cuenta puente\") "
"account entirely when no such entry exists yet or doesn't match. For a "
"bookkeeping flow where bank lines are only ever meant to settle through a "
"receipt/payment order on an outstanding account, keep this enabled to stop "
"automatic reconciliation from ever matching a statement line straight to a "
"receivable/payable account - it still fully reconciles through outstanding "
"accounts, and still falls back to reconcile models either way. Enabled by "
"default, since most of our clients' bookkeeping works this way; disable it "
"for a specific company that settles bank lines directly against invoices/"
"bills instead."
msgstr ""

#. module: account_statement_reconcile_improvements
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:account_statement_reconcile_improvements.res_config_settings_view_form
msgid ""
"Stop automatic bank reconciliation from ever matching a statement line "
"directly against an invoice/bill - only through an outstanding payment/"
"receipt account"
msgstr ""

#. module: account_statement_reconcile_improvements
#: model:ir.model.fields,field_description:account_statement_reconcile_improvements.field_res_company__bank_statement_reconcile_dialog_default_journal
#: model:ir.model.fields,field_description:account_statement_reconcile_improvements.field_res_config_settings__bank_statement_reconcile_dialog_default_journal
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:account_statement_reconcile_improvements.res_config_settings_view_form
msgid "Pre-filter the journal in the reconciliation search dialog"
msgstr ""

#. module: account_statement_reconcile_improvements
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:account_statement_reconcile_improvements.field_res_company__bank_statement_reconcile_dialog_default_journal
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:account_statement_reconcile_improvements.field_res_config_settings__bank_statement_reconcile_dialog_default_journal
msgid ""
"The bank reconciliation screen's own \"Search: Journal Items to Match\" "
"dialog searches every journal by design (useful to catch a payment "
"registered against the wrong bank journal). For a company with many bank "
"journals, that means seeing other banks' candidates mixed in every time. "
"Enabled by default, this pre-selects the journal being reconciled as a "
"search default - still a regular, removable filter, not a restriction. "
"Disable it for a company with few enough journals that the extra "
"candidates are never in the way."
msgstr ""

#. module: account_statement_reconcile_improvements
#: model_terms:ir.ui.view,arch_db:account_statement_reconcile_improvements.res_config_settings_view_form
msgid ""
"Pre-select the journal being reconciled in the \"Search: Journal Items to "
"Match\" dialog - a regular, removable search filter, useful for a company "
"with many bank journals"
msgstr ""

